WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:04.140
The theater industry is going to need&nbsp;
a lot more than a jug of tulkun brain&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.140 --> 00:00:06.840
juice to gain immortality, and Avatar 2's opening&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.840 --> 00:00:09.780
numbers aren't turning out to be the&nbsp;
magic sauce James Cameron hoped for.

00:00:09.780 --> 00:00:14.340
The opening of Avatar: The Way of Water is nothing&nbsp;
to balk at, with the long-in-development sequel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.340 --> 00:00:19.740
raking in more than $400 million worldwide in its&nbsp;
opening weekend, per Box Office Mojo. The numbers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.740 --> 00:00:24.660
however, fell below projections — some of which&nbsp;
had the movie topping $500 million globally.

00:00:24.660 --> 00:00:29.220
The reason this difference matters more in 2022&nbsp;
is that the box office is still trying to make&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.220 --> 00:00:34.200
a full comeback after the shutdowns that stemmed&nbsp;
from the COVID-19 pandemic. To achieve this goal,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:38.220
the U.S. box office is relying on massive&nbsp;
blockbusters like Avatar: The Way of Water,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.220 --> 00:00:42.240
as more and more films — like Halloween&nbsp;
Ends — are released directly to streaming.

00:00:42.240 --> 00:00:46.920
"But the truth is, what we really need&nbsp;
to focus on is getting back to theaters."

00:00:46.920 --> 00:00:51.540
That said, must-see theatrical experiences&nbsp;
that promise to push visual boundaries are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.540 --> 00:00:55.260
still managing to find a place at the box&nbsp;
office. For instance, Top Gun: Maverick&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.260 --> 00:01:01.440
stands as the year's biggest runaway success,&nbsp;
pulling in nearly $1.5 billion worldwide. So,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.440 --> 00:01:06.540
as far as the numbers stand, 2022 proved that&nbsp;
audiences are ready to return to cinemas. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.540 --> 00:01:11.580
2022's domestic financial receipts are&nbsp;
nearly 34% lower than 2019's earnings,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.580 --> 00:01:14.340
meaning that the box office&nbsp;
still has a long way to go.

00:01:14.340 --> 00:01:17.880
For box office purists, Avatar:&nbsp;
The Way of Water was set to change&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.880 --> 00:01:21.540
everything. The film was expected to&nbsp;
be the latest big-screen mega-hit,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.540 --> 00:01:25.800
a juggernaut that would pump new life into&nbsp;
the movie industry. But even the huge opening&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.800 --> 00:01:29.940
of James Cameron's latest blockbuster couldn't&nbsp;
solve the film industry's continuing struggles.

00:01:29.940 --> 00:01:37.020
Avatar: The Way of Water opened to approximately&nbsp;
$134 million domestically and $441 worldwide,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.020 --> 00:01:41.280
per Box Office Mojo. One sign that this&nbsp;
was a disappointing start was the fact that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.280 --> 00:01:46.020
stocks for AMC Entertainment and Cinemark both&nbsp;
dropped on the following Monday. Additionally,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.020 --> 00:01:51.540
stocks for Disney and IMAX also dropped. This&nbsp;
doesn't necessarily spell all bad news for Avatar:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.540 --> 00:01:56.700
The Way of Water as 2009's Avatar only&nbsp;
opened to about $77 million domestically,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.700 --> 00:02:01.260
before earning more than $700 million.&nbsp;
However, it does mean that the movie&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.260 --> 00:02:05.220
was not the last-minute savior the&nbsp;
American box office needed in 2022.

00:02:05.220 --> 00:02:09.540
So, in order to do that, Avatar: The Way of&nbsp;
Water will need to bring people out to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.540 --> 00:02:13.500
movie theater like no other film before&nbsp;
it. According to director James Cameron,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.500 --> 00:02:17.940
the sequel has to break into the top five of the&nbsp;
all-time box office to even be profitable, meaning&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.940 --> 00:02:23.160
it potentially needs to make two billion dollars&nbsp;
worldwide to get into the black. Cameron told GQ:

00:02:23.160 --> 00:02:26.100
"You have to be the third or fourth&nbsp;
highest-grossing film in history.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.100 --> 00:02:28.320
That's your threshold. That's your break even."

00:02:28.870 --> 00:02:32.280
Does a drop in share value after a&nbsp;
less-than-groundbreaking opening for Avatar:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.280 --> 00:02:36.600
The Way of Water mean that movie theaters and&nbsp;
Disney need to worry? Only if they want to breed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.600 --> 00:02:41.340
a larger sense of doom. James Cameron's sequel may&nbsp;
not have brought in over half a billion dollars&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.340 --> 00:02:46.740
during its opening weekend, but it did cross that&nbsp;
mark effortlessly on December 20, 2022, thanks&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.740 --> 00:02:51.780
to international markets like China, India, and&nbsp;
Germany. Just like the first Avatar, the sequel's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.780 --> 00:02:56.280
success relies on its ability to have phenomenal&nbsp;
legs. Cameron himself has even said that the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.280 --> 00:03:00.840
opening weekend shouldn't dictate his film's&nbsp;
success. The director told The Hollywood Reporter:

00:03:00.840 --> 00:03:04.320
"We'll know by the third weekend. You're&nbsp;
not going to know by the first weekend.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:04.320 --> 00:03:07.440
'Titanic' didn't work that way.&nbsp;
'Avatar' didn't work that way."

00:03:07.440 --> 00:03:12.060
However, what Cameron says is far different&nbsp;
from what the industry expects. It would be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.060 --> 00:03:15.720
foolish to speculate how much Avatar: The&nbsp;
Way of Water will rake in, but it's worth&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.720 --> 00:03:20.640
noting that 2023 will be a big year for movie&nbsp;
theaters — so that should quell the anxieties&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.640 --> 00:03:25.500
of shareholders. The first three months of&nbsp;
2023 are filled with blockbuster releases,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:25.500 --> 00:03:29.700
including the Ant-Man threequel,&nbsp;
Creed III, and John Wick: Chapter 4.

00:03:29.700 --> 00:03:33.000
So, even though Avatar: The Way of&nbsp;
Water didn't make the biggest splash,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.000 --> 00:03:36.180
its large debut is still a&nbsp;
promising sign of what's to come.

